From: Lars <118484383+LarzVader@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aic: accept AIC8800D80 revision 7 with the U02 firmware

The RFC v3 BSP only accepts chip_rev 3 (U02). The AIC8800D80 in the Jeazans
C107 tablet reports revision 7 (subrev 0x82); the vendor driver
(aic-bsp-compatible 20231222) loads the U02 firmware set for it, and the
chip works with that under Android. Accept revision 7 the same way.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_bsp/aic_chip_8800d80.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_bsp/aic_chip_8800d80.c
@@ -64,7 +64,12 @@
 
 	aicbsp_info->chip_rev = (u8)((rd_mem_addr_cfm.memdata >> 16) & 0x3F);
 	is_chip_id_h = (u8)(((rd_mem_addr_cfm.memdata >> 16) & 0xC0) == 0xC0);
-	if (is_chip_id_h || aicbsp_info->chip_rev != CHIP_REV_U02) {
+	/*
+	 * Revision 7 (U03) runs the U02 firmware as well, like the vendor driver
+	 * (aic-bsp-compatible 20231222) does on the Jeazans C107 tablet.
+	 */
+	if (is_chip_id_h || (aicbsp_info->chip_rev != CHIP_REV_U02 &&
+			      aicbsp_info->chip_rev != CHIP_REV_U03)) {
 		pr_err("aicbsp: AIC8800D80 U02 is required (revision %u)\n",
 		       aicbsp_info->chip_rev);
 		return -ENODEV;
